{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01NBLE9b9Sds4Xjvhsnt5UAV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good! So `_names_match` is returning `True` for cases like \"Wilson\" matching \"Myrtle Wilson\" (single word matching the last component of multi-word name). The comment at line 579 says \"We NO LONGER match last names here\", but lines 575-585 still match first names.\n\nThe problem is that \"Myrtle\" (single word) matches \"Myrtle Wilson\" (multi-word, first component), which is correct. But then somewhere \"Wilson\" (single word) is also being matched to both \"George Wilson\" and \"Myrtle Wilson\".\n\nLet me check if there's another path where this happens. Let me look at the line 596-602 logic. Actually, I think I see the issue now. Let me check if \"Wilson\" as a single-word name is in the name_groups:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":937,"cache_read_input_tokens":44626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":937,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b290fa2a-4de7-452e-801d-91aeff2d1515","uuid":"dcb3f9a0-f89e-46c9-9403-536b0308c9ed"}
