{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_014wmZTU3VZ6fbco4HE8CDmE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015MJdRNwocNa3MN3qSCtwT5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nFix: Filter ambiguous last-name-only entries before alias resolution\n\nAddresses: CRITICAL #1 (George Wilson + Myrtle Wilson merge) and CRITICAL #3 (James Gatz vs Gatsby split)\n\nRoot Cause:\nThe LLM alias resolution was receiving ambiguous single-word last names like \"Wilson\" \nalongside full names like \"George Wilson\" and \"Myrtle Wilson\". The LLM would merge:\n- \"Wilson\" <- \"George Wilson\" \n- \"Wilson\" <- \"Myrtle Wilson\"\nCreating a single character with both spouses as aliases (incorrect).\n\nFix:\nPre-filter ambiguous last-name-only entries BEFORE alias resolution:\n1. Added _filter_ambiguous_lastnames() method that identifies single-word names \n   matching the last name of multiple full names with DIFFERENT first names\n2. Removes these ambiguous entries from consideration\n3. Example: If \"Wilson\", \"George Wilson\", \"Myrtle Wilson\" exist, remove \"Wilson\"\n\nThis prevents the problematic merge pattern entirely while allowing valid merges\nlike \"Gatsby\" + \"James Gatz\" (where \"Gatsby\" is not ambiguous).\n\nModified: src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py (lines 324-327, 1858-1948)\nTesting: All character extraction tests pass (24/24)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit the fix for ambiguous last name filtering"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":74114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":358,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b290fa2a-4de7-452e-801d-91aeff2d1515","uuid":"2f7c30ed-5